  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR adds `camcraft_geometry::nesting::raster`, slice 1 of the raster nest (#2525). The module is CPU code only. It has no GPU code, no new crate, no new crate edge and no new external dependency.\n\n- `crates/geometry/src/nesting.rs`: the module root (provenance line).\n- `crates/geometry/src/nesting/raster.rs`: `RasterGrid`, `BitRaster`, `RasterError`, the limits and the two public functions.\n- `crates/geometry/src/nesting/raster/scan.rs`: the integer scan conversion.\n- `crates/geometry/tests/nesting_raster.rs`: 10 tests.\n- `docs/decisions/2612-nesting-raster.md`: the unattended decisions.\n\nPublic API:\n\n```rust\npub const DEFAULT_CELL_UNITS: i64; // 1 mm\npub const MAX_CELLS: u64;          // 2^24 (4096 x 4096)\npub const MAX_SIDE: u32;           // 2^16\npub fn cell_units_from_mm(mm: f64) -> Result<i64, RasterError>;\nRasterGrid::new(origin_x, origin_y, cell, width, height) -> Result<RasterGrid, RasterError>;\nRasterGrid::covering(&Region, cell) -> Result<RasterGrid, RasterError>; // origin on the global lattice\npub fn rasterize_over(&Region, &RasterGrid) -> Result<BitRaster, RasterError>; // parts\npub fn rasterize_free(&Region, &RasterGrid) -> Result<BitRaster, RasterError>; // usable sheet\nBitRaster::{grid, words, get, count_ones}\n```\n\nHow it works:\n\n1. The vertices are quantized with the `geo2d` bridge rule (1 unit = 1 um). After that, each cell decision uses exact `i128` arithmetic with checked multiply and add. No float takes part in a cell decision.\n2. Pass \"touched\": each cell whose closed square touches a closed boundary edge. The x extent of an edge in a row slab is rounded outward, and a value on a cell line touches the two cells.\n3. Pass \"centre inside\": even-odd parity of a +x ray at each cell centre, with the half-open edge rule of `geo2d`. Doubled coordinates keep the centre an integer.\n4. Over = touched OR centre inside. Free = centre inside AND NOT touched.\n\nA closed square that meets the region but no edge is fully in the interior, so its centre is inside. Thus \"over\" contains each point of the region. A square with no edge contact and an inside centre is fully in the interior. Thus a \"free\" cell is a true free cell. Holes are not free.\n\nRows are packed in `u32` words (LSB first). Padding bits are zero.\n\nRefusals by name (`RasterError`): `NonPositiveCellSize`, `NonFiniteCellSize`, `GridTooLarge`, `EmptyGrid`, `NonFinite`, `OutOfRange`, `EmptyRegion` (`covering`), `RegionExceedsGrid` (`rasterize_over` refuses a part that does not fit, because a clipped part raster is not an over-approximation). `rasterize_free` clips freely, because a cell outside the region is never free.\n\nNo raster value reaches posted output or a verdict. The raster only filters candidates. The exact `geo2d` check decides (#2525).\n\n## Type\n\n`feat(geometry)`: the module is a new public API of `camcraft-geometry` for the later nest slices. No user sees it yet, and there is no caller.\n\n## Readings (debug build, one thread)\n\n- Part: annulus r = 50 mm, hole r = 20 mm (256 + 64 vertices), cell 0.1 mm: 1000 x 1000 cells, 662620 set, 2.3 ms.\n- Sheet: 3000 x 1500 mm, cell 1 mm (the default): 3000 x 1500 cells, 4491004 free (= 2998 x 1498), 3.9 ms.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/geometry/tests/nesting_raster.rs`, all pass)\n\n- `raster_over_square_golden_and_cover`: golden counts (144 over, 64 free) and the dense-sample cover check.\n- `raster_over_part_with_hole_covers_and_keeps_hole_open`\n- `raster_over_thin_sliver_covers`: a 0.05 mm sliver and a 0.03 mm rotated sliver.\n- `raster_over_rotated_part_covers`: a rotated rectangle and a 17-gon, at 1 mm and at 0.333333 mm.\n- `raster_free_sheet_cells_inside_and_holes_not_free`: each free cell has its four corners and its centre inside, and no edge touches it (exact integer test).\n- `raster_same_input_same_bits`\n- `raster_packing_rows_and_padding`\n- `raster_refusals_name_their_reason`\n- `raster_degenerate_input_is_clean`: empty region, zero-area sliver, region outside the grid, huge coordinates, NaN.\n- `raster_reading_typical_sizes`\n\nQuick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on head `3c3b559bb`: a change to `crates/geometry/src/lib.rs` makes the quick tier fall back to batch. Result: 897 steps, 0 failed, clippy `-D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The cover check uses a dense point sample, not a proof over all points. Points within 0.5 um of a cell line can round to the next cell. The sample offsets keep away from that case.\n- No GPU path, no placer, no Minkowski inflation of a part (later slices of #2525).\n- No release-build timing.\n\n## MCP\n\nNo user-facing command is added, so no MCP tool is owed.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2612\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
